@description "Failover routing: try the primary, fall back to the alternative"

# dispatch.run tries each configured member in order and returns the
# output of the first one that succeeds. Both members are registered
# capabilities; runtime.fail always errors at runtime, so the pipeline falls
# through to runtime.const and returns its value.
#
# Fallback across *missing* capability names is not permitted — a
# name must resolve at compile time. Runtime failure fallback is what
# this example demonstrates.

@assert: result == "I am the fallback!"

{ value: "I am the fallback!" }
-> dispatch.run @{ members: [runtime.fail, runtime.const], payload: . }
